! Two-stage tapered variant of aramis.bmad: the same 6-FODO-cell line, but the last
! two cells' undulators are a SECOND element definition with b_max stepped down 0.4%.
!
! This is the point of driving the FEL from lattice attributes: a heterogeneous line
! is just different elements. Each wiggler carries its own b_max/l_period/field_calc,
! and the tracker derives each segment's aw from the element it is standing in --
! there is no per-segment namelist input. A post-saturation step-down taper like this
! re-matches the resonance to the decelerated beam and pushes power beyond saturation
! (run this example against steady_state to see the difference; numbers in ../README.md).

no_digested
parameter[geometry] = open
parameter[particle] = electron
parameter[e_tot] = 11357.82 * m_electron

! The matched periodic Twiss of this FODO cell at this energy (Genesis's zmatch values,
! the same numbers the benchmark namelists carry). The FEL walk itself never reads
! lattice Twiss; beam_init-driven imports DO -- init_beam_distribution generates
! bunches matched to these.
beginning[beta_a] = 8.53711
beginning[alpha_a] = -0.703306
beginning[beta_b] = 17.3899
beginning[alpha_b] = 1.40348

! Stage 1: aw = 0.84853 (rms, helical), the Benchmark1-SASE undulator.
UND1: wiggler, l = 3.99, l_period = 0.015, field_calc = helical_model, &
      b_max = 0.84853 * (twopi / 0.015) * m_electron / c_light, &
      tracking_method = custom, ds_step = 0.045

! Stage 2: identical device, b_max (hence aw) 0.4% lower.
UND2: UND1, b_max = 0.99600 * 0.84853 * (twopi / 0.015) * m_electron / c_light

D1: drift, l = 0.44
D2: drift, l = 0.24
QF: quadrupole, l = 0.08, k1 = 2.0
QD: quadrupole, l = 0.08, k1 = -2.0

FODO1: line = (UND1, D1, QF, D2, UND1, D1, QD, D2)
FODO2: line = (UND2, D1, QF, D2, UND2, D1, QD, D2)
TAPERED: line = (4*FODO1, 2*FODO2)

use, TAPERED
